# lint-walker-arms allowlist — adjudicated output of tools/walker-arms/walker_arms.py
# (seeded 2026-09-10 from origin/main; every row was read against the C body).
#
# Tab-separated: <key> <class> <reason>. key = <c_file>:<c_function>|<family>|<missing labels>.
# A row also covers any strict subset of its label list (a fix that closes one
# label keeps the rest allowed); a row whose gap is gone is a stale NOTE, delete it.
#
# Classes (the task's triage vocabulary):
#   UNPORTED   the node type / feature is not constructed in pgrust (CustomScan
#              providers are C extension hooks; postgres_fdw EPQ join alternatives
#              are not generated; PARAM_MULTIEXPR deparse is unported)
#   ELSEWHERE  handled by a different structure: a pre-dispatch check, a helper
#              (strip_relabel, strip_assignment_indirection), a typed enum
#              variant, a different owner (HashJoin owns its Hash child), or the
#              same tag guarded by a field the C arm also tests
#   NOOP       the C arms are `break` / Assert(false) / elog(ERROR) fallthroughs
#              whose behaviour the Rust wildcard already reproduces
#   UNREACHABLE the C arm cannot be reached from SQL in this tree (with the
#              reason); a real divergence would need a new entry point first
#
# Add a row only after reading the C arm. Prefer porting the arm C-exactly.
src/backend/utils/adt/ruleutils.c:get_name_for_var_field|RTEKind|RTE_FUNCTION,RTE_GROUP,RTE_NAMEDTUPLESTORE,RTE_RELATION,RTE_RESULT,RTE_TABLEFUNC,RTE_VALUES	NOOP	every missing C arm is a bare `break` (ruleutils.c get_name_for_var_field); Rust `_ => {}` is the same fallthrough; witness: fixtures/walker-arms-witness.sql
src/backend/optimizer/prep/prepjointree.c:replace_vars_in_jointree|RTEKind|RTE_CTE,RTE_GROUP,RTE_JOIN,RTE_NAMEDTUPLESTORE,RTE_RESULT	NOOP	C arms are Assert(false) "these shouldn't be marked LATERAL"; Rust wildcard skips them the same way; witness: fixtures/walker-arms-witness.sql
src/backend/parser/parse_target.c:FigureColnameInternal|SubLinkType|ALL_SUBLINK,ANY_SUBLINK,CTE_SUBLINK,MULTIEXPR_SUBLINK,ROWCOMPARE_SUBLINK	NOOP	C arms are `break` (unnamed sublink kinds); Rust `_ => 0`; witness: fixtures/walker-arms-witness.sql
src/backend/executor/nodeAgg.c:ExecAgg|AggStrategy|AGG_MIXED,AGG_PLAIN	ELSEWHERE	exec_agg branches on gsets/perhash instead of aggstrategy: AGG_MIXED only arises with grouping sets (gsets::exec_agg_gsets), AGG_PLAIN/AGG_SORTED share the retrieve-direct tail; witness: fixtures/walker-arms-witness.sql
src/backend/optimizer/prep/prepjointree.c:pull_up_simple_subquery|RTEKind|RTE_NAMEDTUPLESTORE	NOOP	C arm is `break` ("can't contain lateral references"); Rust `_ => {}`; witness: fixtures/walker-arms-witness.sql
src/backend/optimizer/plan/createplan.c:create_plan_recurse|NodeTag|T_Agg,T_Append,T_BitmapHeapScan,T_CustomScan,T_ForeignScan,T_Gather,T_GatherMerge,T_Group,T_HashJoin,T_IncrementalSort,T_IndexOnlyScan,T_IndexScan,T_Limit,T_LockRows,T_Material,T_Memoize,T_MergeAppend,T_MergeJoin,T_ModifyTable,T_NestLoop,T_ProjectSet,T_RecursiveUnion,T_SetOp,T_Sort,T_SubqueryScan,T_TidRangeScan,T_TidScan,T_Unique,T_WindowAgg	ELSEWHERE	C switches on Path.pathtype (plan-node tags); Rust dispatches on the PathNode variant, which is a bijection onto the same arms (createplan.rs create_plan_recurse); CustomScan is UNPORTED; witness: fixtures/walker-arms-witness.sql
src/backend/optimizer/plan/createplan.c:create_join_plan|NodeTag|T_HashJoin,T_MergeJoin,T_NestLoop	ELSEWHERE	C switches on pathtype T_HashJoin/T_MergeJoin/T_NestLoop; Rust dispatches on PathNode::HashPath/MergePath/NestPath; witness: fixtures/walker-arms-witness.sql
src/backend/executor/execExpr.c:ExecInitExprRec|NodeTag|T_AggState,T_WindowAggState	ELSEWHERE	C tests IsA(state->parent, AggState/WindowAggState) to find the owning node; init_expr_rec receives the aggregate binding as the `agg: Option<Bind>` parameter (execexpr/compile.rs); witness: fixtures/walker-arms-witness.sql
src/backend/nodes/nodeFuncs.c:expression_tree_mutator_impl|NodeTag|T_IndexClause,T_PlaceHolderInfo	ELSEWHERE	IndexClause and PlaceHolderInfo are planner arena structs, not Node variants, in pgrust (nodes_core/src/lib.rs); their rinfo/indexquals/ph_var are walked by the owning planner code; witness: fixtures/walker-arms-witness.sql
src/backend/nodes/nodeFuncs.c:expression_tree_walker_impl|NodeTag|T_IndexClause,T_PlaceHolderInfo	ELSEWHERE	IndexClause and PlaceHolderInfo are planner arena structs, not Node variants, in pgrust (nodes_core/src/lib.rs); their rinfo/indexquals/ph_var are walked by the owning planner code; witness: fixtures/walker-arms-witness.sql
src/backend/optimizer/path/allpaths.c:set_rel_consider_parallel|RTEKind|RTE_GROUP,RTE_JOIN	NOOP	C arms are Assert(false) "shouldn't happen"; Rust wildcard panics the same way; witness: fixtures/walker-arms-witness.sql
src/backend/executor/execAmi.c:ExecRestrPos|NodeTag|T_CustomScanState	UNPORTED	CustomScan providers are C extension hooks; pgrust never constructs a CustomScan/CustomScanState
src/backend/optimizer/path/costsize.c:cost_qual_eval_walker|NodeTag|T_RestrictInfo	ELSEWHERE	RestrictInfo is not dispatched as a Node in pgrust: callers pass rinfo.clause and the eval_cost cache lives on the RestrictInfo (costsize/src/lib.rs cost_qual_eval); witness: fixtures/walker-arms-witness.sql
src/backend/optimizer/plan/createplan.c:create_scan_plan|NodeTag|T_CustomScan	UNPORTED	CustomScan providers are C extension hooks; pgrust never constructs a CustomScan
